From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:51:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] zink: keep at most 32 MiB of unused buffers in the cache

Zink sized the cache of freed buffers at an eighth of the memory its driver
reports.  KosmicKrisp reports the host's physical memory as its one heap, so
the bound followed the machine: 8 GiB on a Mac with 64 GiB and 512 MiB on an
iPad mini with 4 GiB.  The cache holds what a client freed for as long as
nobody adds or reclaims, so a bound that large kept whatever a burst of
allocation left, and a run on the Mac read different memory from the same run
on the iPad.  Measured at idle on a Retina Android guest, the buffers cached
five seconds after the apps closed were about 75 MiB.

The limit is now the smaller of an eighth of the reported memory and 32 MiB.
A launch or a scroll reuses buffers of the display's size, a few full-screen
buffers of 3 to 12 MiB, and a buffer larger than the limit is destroyed
instead of cached, as it was against a limit it exceeded.  ZINK_BO_CACHE_MAX_MIB
changes the 32 for a run and 0 keeps nothing, so that a launch, a scroll or a
WebGL page can be compared across values with one build.  The topic stands
apart from the one that frees expired buffers so that the value can be
retuned, or the cap dropped, without touching the reaper.

zink_bo_init() asserts that the limit it gave the cache is at most an eighth
of the reported memory, and pb_cache_add_buffer() asserts that the cache
never holds more than its limit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_bo.c | 26 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_bo.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_bo.c
index 77dda0f4f862f8252cb2b7a5f557af34e6fb5875..959b93471324b155517c28db036056c61fdb501e 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_bo.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_bo.c
@@ -1364,6 +1364,28 @@ bo_slab_alloc_normal(void *priv, unsigned mem_type_idx, unsigned entry_size, uns
    return bo_slab_alloc(priv, mem_type_idx, entry_size, group_index, false);
 }
 
+/* The most memory the cache keeps of buffers nobody uses.  A host driver that
+ * reports its physical memory as one heap, as KosmicKrisp does, makes a
+ * fraction of the heap a bound that follows the machine: 8 GiB on a Mac with
+ * 64 GiB and 512 MiB on an iPad with 4 GiB.  A fixed bound is the same on
+ * both, and what a launch or a scroll reuses is a few buffers of the display's
+ * size.  ZINK_BO_CACHE_MAX_MIB changes it for a run, and 0 keeps none. */
+#define ZINK_BO_CACHE_MAX_MIB 32
+
+static uint64_t
+zink_bo_cache_limit(uint64_t total_mem)
+{
+   long max_mib = debug_get_num_option("ZINK_BO_CACHE_MAX_MIB",
+                                       ZINK_BO_CACHE_MAX_MIB);
+
+   if (max_mib < 0)
+      max_mib = ZINK_BO_CACHE_MAX_MIB;
+   /* Keep the shift below 64 bits whatever the environment says. */
+   max_mib = MIN2(max_mib, (long)UINT32_MAX);
+
+   return MIN2(total_mem / 8, (uint64_t)max_mib << 20);
+}
+
 bool
 zink_bo_init(struct zink_screen *screen)
 {
@@ -1373,8 +1395,10 @@ zink_bo_init(struct zink_screen *screen)
    /* Create managers. */
    pb_cache_init(&screen->pb.bo_cache, screen->info.mem_props.memoryTypeCount,
                  500000, 1.5f, 0,
-                 total_mem / 8, offsetof(struct zink_bo, cache_entry), screen,
+                 zink_bo_cache_limit(total_mem),
+                 offsetof(struct zink_bo, cache_entry), screen,
                  (void*)bo_destroy, (void*)bo_can_reclaim);
+   assert(screen->pb.bo_cache.max_cache_size <= total_mem / 8);
    /* Not having a reaper only costs memory a client that stopped allocating
     * leaves cached. */
    screen->pb.bo_reaper = pb_cache_reaper_create(&screen->pb.bo_cache, "zink-bo-cache");
